		<td width="100%">
			<table width="100%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="2" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%" class="title" colspan="2">Level Guides</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3513">mezmrizr</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">2/7/2002 - 6:39 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
										
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														ok heres the idea,everyone post there places/areas that they have found for good xp and good loot, to help others,like me for instance,im tired of DL and want to get to 45 soon,hehe,anyway if u think its a good idea post some						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3023">Maysun</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">2/11/2002 - 7:23 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2670">Maysun Researcher</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2733">Olloder</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2950">Shantillie</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Kedge Keep, 40 to 55 in a group. Experience is awesome. Loot is bad unless you are targeting a specific item.<br />
<br />
Burning Woods 40 to 50+. Killing Hornets(Hotwings) Loot is good experiece can be good with a fast group.<br />
<br />
Great Divide Killing giants, with a good group xp isn't so bad, loot is fair.<br />
<br />
For those with Luclin, Scarlet Desert, Twilight Sea, Dawnshroud Peaks, Tenebrous Mountains, Mons Letalis, 40 to 50+ all good xp with a group. Loot varies on zone, at best it is fair.<br />
<br />
30 to 45 Stonebrunt Mountains, loot is fair to good depending on what's hunted. (Panda's have dropped gems worth over 50pp, but they are still light blue to Maysun at 51). Also the titans are there and can be very dangerous. XP is good.<br />
<br />
If you are after coin loot, Rathe Mountains for HG's, but it always seems over crowded.<br />
<br />
Hope some of these suggestions help.						</td>
					</tr>
										<tr>
						<td class="body" align="left">
							<br>
							<div class="xsmall">
							<i>Edited by <a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3023">Maysun</a> on 2/11/2002 - 7:24 AM PST</i>
							</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3485">aamilea</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">2/25/2002 - 3:27 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2788">Aamilea</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														stonebrunt=pelt heaven. tailors should hunt there. for someone with track and animal fear, like Raija, you can haul away xp and backpack full of pelts.<br />
<br />
3 days of camping, i have 7 stacks of LQ pelt for leatherpadding. before skinning, the distribution was like. 12HQ, 2.5 stacks MQ and the rest LQ, and no ruinned ones. those cats are well groomed.<br />
<br />
Kedge Keep=good suggestion. i've always wanted to go there but never been....						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3597">Kaledine</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">2/25/2002 - 6:10 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2879">Kaledine Ursamaje</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2917">Karuune Bogglesworth</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2918">Dambae Meadowlark</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														To be honest, some of the best experience I got between 35 and 45 (even in hell) was in City of Mist, but that's someplace you need to have a ready-made group for.  If you can gather the group (including a cleric, lol...as an enchanter, you'll be getting hit a lot, and not out of admiration) together, you'll find you can get some great experience there, and if you're lucky, MOST of the items that can be acquired here can be found on any mob.  Just don't go in past the entrance, and you'll be fine.<br />
<br />
In Luclin, Dawnshroud Peaks, if you can get a group there, is good experience.  Not sure about the loot, though.  Twilight Sea is great experience, and the loot is amazing!<br />
<br />
In Velious, Great Divide is ok experience, the loot isn't so good, and it gets boring early on, but on the other hand, you'll want the faction hits if you want to ally yourself with the shorties and those-who-ate-too-much-hot-sauce.  If you can get a wurm group (and you can...you're an enchanter, lol), the loot is decent, and the guardians and ancients drop spells.  The rygorr fort is good experience, as well as Crystal Caverns, where the loot is damned good for the level of the place, not to mention the experience bonus.  (I put on a yellow and a half in 35 hell on Dambae in about 3 hours there.)  Just don't fight the geonids, because, as a pure caster, I believe you'll need them for a quest later on.<br />
<br />
Ok, I think I've overstayed my proverbial welcome.  I hope I've given you some food for thought, as I know I got very bored in DL on Kale when she was 40th, and these were some of the places that alleviated my boredom.<br />
<br />
*Steps off of her soapbox*<br />
<br />
Kaledine Ursamaje, 51st Witch Doctor<br />
Karuune Bogglesworth, 45th Crack Whore<br />
Dambae Meadowlark, 39th Port Bitch<br />
Kylrene (soon to be Jin'Rah), 20th Sour Note						</td>
